chances are you know someone suffering  from back or neck pain two-thirds of  adults suffer from some level or back or  neck pain at some point in their lives  one of the most common causes of back  and neck pain is degeneration of the  discs the shock absorbers that act as  padding between each link in the spine  the typical surgical treatments for a  degenerated discs are expensive painful  and can actually cause other nearby  discs to break down over time now a team  of researchers have developed a new  technique to grow engineered discs in  the lab first they seeded a disc made of  a hydrogel polymer with stem cells taken  from a goat the seeded disc was then  sandwiched between two pieces of foam  made from a polymer called  polycaprolactone the researchers  implanted the lab-grown discs into the  necks of goats the discs were subjected  to periodic compression tests to compare  their performance to natural ones  researchers found that after eight weeks  the engineered discs ability to  withstand compression became just as  good as the natural discs all of the  goats recovered from the implantation  surgery without complication a possessed  full range of motion and their necks  throughout the study duration we are  unfortunately a long way off from human  trials researchers would like to  continue long term studies of the  effectiveness of the discs and goats and  other larger mammals still this could  mean that in the future those with  end-stage disc degeneration would be  able to turn to discs grown in a lab to  ease their suffering  [Music]  [Music]
 

